import Work.XHostT.TScratch

/-!
# (key: bridge-host-cross) The network with other providers (`XNet.withIc`) and with private scratch (`XNet.reC`)

Field-by-field copies of p-a3's `XNet` (generated by p-disp/tools/gen_tdispw.py from TDef.lean's field list, 141
fields):
* `XNet.withIc N Ic' htv hent`: the same network whose call `(ρ, l)` runs `Ic' ρ l`, for invocations with the same
  target vectors and the same ENTRANCE LABELS as `N`'s (so every frame, host chain and bank of `N` is unchanged);
  `unit_withIc`: the price changes by the calls only;
* `XNet.reC N e`: every call of `N` with its copies re-indexed by `e : C ↪ C'` (`GInvE.reC`), the copies outside the
  image of `e` private scratch of every call; EVERY other field is `N`'s (host table, banks, host chains, pads,
  remainders), so the host check is the same, and `unit_reC : (N.reC e).unit φ = N.unit φ` (`rfl`);
* **`xnet_disp_scratch_certificate`**: two providers dispatched by a table AND private scratch per call;
* `xnet_withIc_certificate`, `xnet_reC_certificate`.
Written by p-disp (wht45/lever, 19 Oct 2026); prepared with assistance from Claude.  No `sorry`.
-/

